          %p Discussion of the early history:
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#Kosinski93"} Kosinski 93, Section IX.9
          %h5#TwistedEquivariantPontrjaginConstruction Twisted/equivariant generalizations
          %p
            The (fairly straightforward) generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Pontrjagin+theorem"} twisted Pontrjagin theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+twisted-framed+submanifolds"} normally twisted-framed submanifolds
          %ul
            %li#Cruickshank03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Cruickshank"}> James Cruickshank
              , Lemma 5.2 using Sec. 5.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twisted homotopy theory and the geometric equivariant 1-stem
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0166-8641(02)00183-9"} doi:10.1016/S0166-8641(02)00183-9
          %p
            A general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Pontrjagin+theorem"} equivariant Pontrjagin theorem
            – relating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Cohomotopy"} equivariant Cohomotopy
            to normal equivariant framed submanifolds – remains elusive, but on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifolds"} G-manifolds
            it is again straightforward (and reduces to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Pontrjagin+theorem"} twisted Pontrjagin theorem
            on the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
          %ul
            %li#Cruickshank99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Cruickshank"}> James Cruickshank
              , Thm. 5.0.6, Cor. 6.0.13 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twisted Cobordism and its Relationship to Equivariant Homotopy Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/s4/f2/dsk1/tape9/PQDD_0030/NQ46823.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Cruickshank99.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %h5#InNegativeCodimension In negative codimension
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+charge+map"} Cohomotopy charge map
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
            gives the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "configuration+space+of+points#LoopSpacesOfSuspensions"} May-Segal theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"} Cohomotopy
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle+spaces"} cocycle spaces
            with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
          %ul
            %li#May72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of iterated loop spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/geom_iter.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Segal73
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Configuration-spaces and iterated loop-spaces
                %strong 21
                (1973), 213–221. MR 0331377 (
                %a{:href => "http://dodo.pdmi.ras.ru/~topology/books/segal.pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p c Generalization of these constructions and results is due to
            %li#McDuff75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dusa+McDuff"}> Dusa McDuff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Configuration spaces of positive and negative particles
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(75)90038-5"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(75)90038-5
            %li#Boedigheimer87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carl-Friedrich+B%C3%B6digheimer"}> Carl-Friedrich Bödigheimer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable splittings of mapping spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~cfb/PUBLICATIONS/stable-splittings-of-mapping-spaces.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BoedigheimerStableSplittings87.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %h4#thoms_construction Thom’s construction
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"} Thom's theorem
            i.e. the unstable and
            %em oriented
            version of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+construction"} Pontrjagin-Thom construction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+oriented+submanifolds"} normally oriented submanifolds
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+vector+bundle"} universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M SO(n)
          %ul
            %li#Thom54
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ren%C3%A9+Thom"}> René Thom
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quelques+propri%C3%A9t%C3%A9s+globales+des+vari%C3%A9t%C3%A9s+diff%C3%A9rentiables"} Quelques propriétés globales des variétés différentiables
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02566923"} doi:10.1007/BF02566923
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/139072"} dml:139072
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.digizeitschriften.de/dms/img/?PID=GDZPPN002056259"} digiz:GDZPPN002056259
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/thomcob.pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Stong68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Stong"}> Robert Stong
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on Cobordism theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://pi.math.virginia.edu/StongConf/Stongbookcontents.pdf"} toc pdf
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "http://press.princeton.edu/titles/6465.html"} publisher page
          %h4#lashofs_construction Lashof’s construction
          %p
            The joint generalization of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Pontryagin38a"} Pontryagin 38a
            %a{:href => "#Pontryagin55"} 55
            (framing structure) and
            %a{:href => "#Thom54"} Thom 54
            (orientation structure) to any family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structures"} tangential structures
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28B%2Cf%29-structure"}> (B,f)-structure
            ”) is first made explicit in
          %ul
            %li#Lashof63
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Lashof"}> Richard Lashof
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Poincaré duality and cobordism
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1963-0156357-4"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-1963-0156357-4
          %p
            and the general statement that has come to be known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+isomorphism"} Pontryagin-Thom isomorphism
            (identifying the stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of normally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structure"} (B,f)-structured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mf"} Mf
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lashof63"} Lashof 63, Theorem C
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodor+Br%C3%B6cker"}> Theodor Bröcker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"} Tammo tom Dieck
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kobordismentheorie
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 178
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9783540053415"} ISBN:9783540053415
            %li#Kochman96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
                , section 1.5 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
            %li#Rudyak98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuli+Rudyak"}> Yuli Rudyak
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Thom spectra, orientability and cobordism
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/rudyakthom.pdf"} pdf
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
                ,
                %em Topology of manifolds
                course notes (2010) (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/"}> web
                ), Lecture 3:
                %em Thom’s theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/3thom.pdf"}> pdf
                ), Lecture 4
                %em Transversality
                (notes by I. Bobkova) (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/4transversality.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Malkiewich11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
                , Section 3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Unoriented cobordism and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mi O
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.math.binghamton.edu/malkiewich/cobordism.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Tom Weston, Part I of
                %em An introduction to cobordism theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://people.math.umass.edu/~weston/oldpapers/cobord.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manifold+Atlas"}> Manifold Atlas
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://web.archive.org/web/20250310110744/http://www.map.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/B-Bordism#The_Pontrjagin-Thom_isomorphism"} The Pontrjagin-Thom isomorphism
